prisma/seed-blog-wave3-wave4-games.ts:653:- **Combined Status** — adds exact temperature, current season, and days-remaining-in-season readouts to your HUD. DST hides a surprising amount of useful information by default, and this mod surfaces it without changing any gameplay mechanics.
prisma/seed-blog-wave3-wave4-games.ts:657:- **The Engineer** — a custom playable character mod with over 160,000 Workshop subscribers, making it the highest-rated character mod in DST's ecosystem by a wide margin. If your group wants a new character to try beyond the base roster, this is the safest, most-tested pick rather than a random low-subscriber option.
prisma/seed-blog-wave3-wave4-games.ts:661:Unlike some titles in this list, DST mod installation on a dedicated server is Klei's own well-documented system:
prisma/seed-blog-wave3-wave4-games.ts:666:4. Restart the server — DST will download and load the mods automatically.
prisma/seed-blog-wave3-wave4-games.ts:674:With 15,000+ mods on the Workshop, subscriber count and recent-update date are your best filters — the Workshop page for each mod shows both directly. A mod with tens of thousands of subscribers and an update within the last content patch cycle is a far safer bet than a low-subscriber mod that hasn't been touched since an old game version, since DST updates can silently break older mods until their authors catch up. The mods above (ActionQueue Reborn, Combined Status, The Engineer) all pass that bar comfortably.
prisma/seed-blog-wave3-wave4-games.ts:678:Before any of this matters, your DST dedicated server needs a **cluster token** generated from your Klei account — without it, the server won't run publicly at all. Generate it from Klei's account services page while logged into the same account you play under, then save it as \`cluster_token.txt\` in your cluster's root folder. This is a one-time setup step, but it's the single most common thing new DST server owners miss, since nothing else on the setup checklist depends on a linked account the way this does.
prisma/seed-blog-wave3-wave4-games.ts:682:DST is one of the lighter titles here to host, even with mods:
prisma/seed-blog-wave3-wave4-games.ts:690:Klei ships regular content updates to DST (new seasonal events, characters and refreshes), and each one is a moment where installed mods can briefly go stale until their authors catch up. Rather than auto-updating your server the instant a patch drops, many long-running DST communities wait a day or two after a major update — long enough for the Workshop mods they depend on to get a compatibility fix — before rolling their own cluster forward. It's a small habit that avoids a surprising number of "why did my modded server just break" moments.
